  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {"@type":"Question","name":"What BLDC motor do I need for a warehouse AGV?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Warehouse AGVs carrying 500-2000 kg typically use dual 200-750W BLDC gear motors. For pallet truck-style AGVs (2000 kg), dual 500W motors with 30:1 planetary gear provide 1.0-1.5 m/s travel speed and 5% gradient climbing. For smaller goods-to-person robots (50-300 kg), 100-200W motors are sufficient."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"How do I choose between L-type and R-type drive motors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"R-type (coaxial/inline) motors align the motor shaft with the wheel shaft, giving the most compact wheel module — ideal for tight AGV chassis where height is limited. L-type (right-angle) motors position the motor perpendicular to the wheel, saving vertical space but requiring more lateral clearance. For forklift AGVs and pallet trucks, L-type is common. For flat mobile robots, R-type is preferred."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"What IP rating for warehouse drive motors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"IP54 minimum for standard indoor warehouses. IP65 for cold storage, food processing, and pharmaceutical warehouses with regular washdown. Cold storage applications also require low-temperature grease (rated to -30°C) and heaters on motor windings to prevent condensation."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"How long do BLDC drive motors last in warehouse AGVs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"BLDC drive motors typically last 20,000-30,000 operating hours in AGV applications, equivalent to 5-8 years of 16h/day operation. The primary wear item is the gearbox bearings, not the motor itself. Planetary gearboxes should be inspected every 10,000 hours. Compared to brushed DC motors (3000-5000 hour brush life), BLDC motors reduce maintenance downtime by 80%."}},
    {"@type":"Question","name":"Can I use the same motor for drive and steering?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Drive and steering motors have different requirements. Drive motors need high torque at low-to-medium speed (0.5-2.0 m/s). Steering motors need precise positioning (±0.5°) at very low speed. Shenghe Zhilian offers matched drive-and-steer motor pairs designed to integrate into standard AGV wheel modules with compatible controllers."}}
