    <h2>L-Type vs R-Type: Choosing the Right Form Factor</h2>
    <p><strong>R-type (coaxial):</strong> Motor axis aligns with wheel shaft. Lowest profile, most compact wheel module. Preferred for flat mobile robots (goods-to-person, sorting) where chassis height is critical. Available in 120-750W at Shenghe Zhilian.</p>
    <p><strong>L-type (right-angle):</strong> Motor perpendicular to wheel shaft. More lateral space needed but shorter axial length. Preferred for pallet trucks and forklift AGVs where the motor sits above or beside the wheel. Available in 120-1,500W.</p>
    <p>Both types use <a href="/blog/bldc-motor-sizing-agv/">BLDC motors with planetary gear reducers</a> for high efficiency (92-97%) and backdrivability (important for safety — the robot can be pushed by hand when power is off).</p>

    <h2>Battery Life Optimization</h2>
    <p>In warehouse operations, AGVs run 16-20 hours per day with fast-charging breaks. Motor efficiency directly impacts battery size, charging frequency, and operating cost.</p>
    <p>A warehouse AGV with dual 400W drive motors running at average 60% load for 16 hours:</p>
    <p><strong>BLDC (91% efficiency):</strong> 2 × 400 × 0.6 / 0.91 × 16 = 8,439 Wh/day = 8.4 kWh battery. <strong>Brushed DC (70% efficiency):</strong> 2 × 400 × 0.6 / 0.70 × 16 = 10,971 Wh/day = 11.0 kWh battery.</p>
    <p>The BLDC system needs a <strong>23% smaller battery</strong> — saving $500-1,500 in battery cost per robot, reducing weight by 5-8 kg, and extending time between charges by 30-40 minutes.</p>

    <h2>Cold Storage and Special Environments</h2>
    <p><strong>Cold storage (-25°C to -30°C):</strong> Standard motor grease solidifies below -20°C, causing high starting torque and premature bearing failure. Cold storage AGV motors require: synthetic low-temperature grease (rated to -40°C), winding heaters to prevent condensation during warm-up, and IP65 sealing to prevent ice formation on internal components.</p>
    <p><strong>Cleanroom (pharmaceutical/electronics):</strong> Motors must be fully enclosed (IP65+) with smooth, wipeable surfaces. No exposed fasteners or crevices that trap particles. Outgassing certification may be required for semiconductor cleanrooms.</p>
    <p><strong>Food-grade warehouses:</strong> IP65 with food-safe lubricant. Stainless steel mounting hardware. Motors must be compatible with regular washdown cleaning.</p>

